          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Feb 24 2026 23:28:54 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Stryker’s integrated operating room is featured in a newly published industry supplement spotlighting how connected operating room technologies can help advance efficiency, collaboration and surgical care.<sup>1</sup> As healthcare systems continue to seek smarter, more streamlined environments, the article explores the growing need for integrated OR solutions that bring people, technology and information together.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">At the heart of this story is <span class=\"futura-bold\">Created to Connect</span> - the integrated vision behind the iSuite. Designed to unify the OR experience, Stryker’s integrated iSuite helps support more connected workflows, improved coordination across care teams and a modern surgical environment built for the future.<sup>1</sup></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The feature reinforces Stryker’s commitment to helping operating rooms run more efficiently while empowering clinicians to focus on what matters most: patient care.</span><br>\n</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><a href=\"https://www.ormanagement.net/Monographs-and-Whitepapers/Article/03-26/Operating-Room-Efficiency-Stryker-iSuite-Advancing-Surgical-Care/79986\"><span class=\"standalone-link\">Read the full supplement here</span></a></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon May 18 2026 17:50:23 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
